From cb59afddd94afdc0bc7ed1f8975121c1f7660b37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c <a@b>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: report both operating systems even when one fails

WHAT THIS IS
    The matrix of the desktop test workflow had no `fail-fast: false`,
    so GitHub cancelled the other job of the matrix when one of them
    failed, and the result of the second operating system was never
    reported. A Linux only problem could hide a Windows only problem.

WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT THE WORKFLOW FILE
    The GitHub App that pushes this repository has no `workflows`
    permission, so it cannot write `.github/workflows/`. This change
    therefore travels as a patch, and the owner applies it once.

    `patches/ci-libegl-failfast.patch` used to add these very same
    lines byte for byte, so applying both of them was impossible. The
    two no longer collide: this one carries the matrix setting and the
    other one carries the Qt runtime libraries.

---
 .github/workflows/tests.yml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/tests.yml b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
index 3862b81..b2470d7 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/tests.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@ permissions:
 jobs:
   test:
     strategy:
+      # Report both operating systems even when one fails, so a Linux only
+      # problem never hides the Windows result.
+      fail-fast: false
       matrix:
         os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest]
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
